# Castafiore - Session Log

## 2026-08-05 (7th)
- Mini-player swipe fixes (TODO #3 follow-up):
  - **Bug fix**: horizontal swipe worked only once — the `PanResponder` (created once via
    `useRef`) captured the *initial* `song`/`config`. After the first gesture `song.index` had
    advanced, but the stale closure called `nextSong(..., oldSong, ...)` which set the same index
    again → "stuck on the same song". Fixed by reading `songRef.current` / `configRef.current`
    (refs updated every render) inside the responder.
  - Removed the swipe-down dismiss + `BoxPlayerBubble` restore (user request): deleted
    `BoxPlayerBubble.js`, dropped `isHidden` state from `Player.js`, removed the `onDismiss`
    branch. Vertical swipe now only expands; horizontal = next/prev (repeatable).

## 2026-08-05 (6th)
- Server binding extended to cellular data (TODO #5 follow-up). Plan: `plans/cellular-network-binding.md`.
- `utils/network.native.js`: added `getNetworkInfo()` → `{type:'wifi',ssid}|{type:'cellular'}|{type:'none'}`
  (`NetInfo.fetch()` no-arg) + exported `CELLULAR_NETWORK = '__cellular__'` token; `getCurrentNetwork()`
  is now a ssid-only wrapper. Web stub returns `{type:'none'}` + token export.
- `networkAutoSwitch.js` `decide()`: on cellular → match server with `network === CELLULAR_NETWORK`;
  on wifi → match by ssid (skips the token). Leaving a bound network (wifi OR cellular) → fallback
  (lastFallback, else first server without a binding). Old gap fixed: leaving a bound WiFi for
  cellular used to do nothing (short-circuited on null ssid) — now it falls back.
- `AddServer.js`: "Cellular data" chip (`mobile` icon) alongside the SSID chips; field shows the
  translated label while bound to cellular; `settings.networks` history keeps only real SSIDs.
- `Connect.js`: cellular-bound servers show a `mobile` icon instead of `wifi`.
- i18n en/de: `Network (WiFi)` → `Network`; added `Cellular`.
- eslint clean; APK rebuilt (1m25s) + installed on R5CY71GYKWF.

